{"study_accession":"PRJNA683207","secondary_study_accession":"SRP296987","title":"Novel LncRNA and mRNA expression profiles of peripheral blood mononuclear cells in patients with systemic lupus erythematosus and healthy controls","description":"The multi-system involvement and high heterogeneity lead to great challenge in the diagnosis and treatment of systemic lupus erythematosus (SLE). Long non-coding RNA is a type of RNA greater than 200 nucleotides that does not encode proteins. LncRNA is a key regulator of gene expression in the immune system and is involved in the pathogenesis of a variety of autoimmune diseases, including SLE. In this work, we performed transcriptome sequencing and microarray analysis of peripheral blood mononuclear cells (PBMC) from freshly isolated healthy controls (n=5) and SLE patients (n=5) to analyze the expression of novel lncRNAs and mRNAsand explore their potential as biomarkers and their correlation with clinical features. Overall design: PBMCs were isolated from 5 healthy controls and 5 patients with SLE, and total RNA was extracted for transcriptome sequencing [Dec-28-2022] The submitter corrected the annotation of GSM4962537-GSM4962541 from healthy controls to SLE patients and of GSM4962542-GSM4962546 from SLE patients to healthy controls.","pubmed":"34150746","geo_series":"","n_samples":10,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN17024080","study_accession":"PRJNA683207","blood_class":"pbmc","class_from":"sample","title":"SLE patient 1_SLE1","description":"SLE patient 1_SLE1","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM4962537","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2021-01-07","attributes":[["source_name","systemic lupus erythematosus"],["disease","systemic lupus erythematosus"],["tissue","Peripheral Blood"],["cell_type","PBMCs"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR13214141","experiment_accession":"SRX9647186","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000","read_count":37505935,"base_count":11